from (values
('115.27.b.5.C',3,'Which statement about childhood trauma is accurate?','["It is never talked about at school", "Only weak people are affected", "It always ruins a person''s life", "People can heal and recover with support"]'::jsonb,3,'Support and treatment promote recovery.','original'),
('115.27.b.6.A',3,'A way to support a friend with a long-term illness such as asthma is to...','["be understanding and learn how to help in an emergency", "tease them about it", "avoid them", "tell them to stop using medicine"]'::jsonb,0,'Support means understanding and being prepared.','original'),
('115.27.b.6.A',3,'A classmate has type 1 diabetes. A caring way to support them is to...','["dare them to skip insulin", "respect their need for breaks to check blood sugar", "call them lazy", "tell the whole school"]'::jsonb,1,'Respect and patience help.','original'),
('115.27.b.6.B',3,'Promoting resiliency in a stressed friend can include...','["pressuring them to ignore their feelings", "joking about their problem", "listening and encouraging them to use healthy coping skills", "telling them to tough it out alone"]'::jsonb,2,'Support builds resilience.','original'),
('115.27.b.6.B',3,'Which action positively influences peers?','["excluding someone online", "laughing at a mistake", "spreading a rumor", "inviting a left-out classmate to join your table"]'::jsonb,3,'Inclusion helps well-being.','original'),
('115.27.b.6.C',3,'A healthy self-management strategy for stress is...','["exercise, sleep and talking to a trusted person", "isolating completely", "using substances", "skipping meals"]'::jsonb,0,'Healthy habits reduce stress.','original'),
('115.27.b.6.C',3,'Which is an unhealthy way to cope with anxiety?','["going for a walk", "using alcohol or other drugs to numb feelings", "practicing deep breathing", "journaling"]'::jsonb,1,'Substance use is unhealthy and can worsen anxiety.','original'),
('115.27.b.6.D',3,'Which is a physical consequence of an eating disorder?','["stronger immune system", "better concentration", "heart and bone problems from poor nutrition", "increased height"]'::jsonb,2,'Eating disorders can cause serious medical complications.','original'),
('115.27.b.6.D',3,'A friend shows signs of an eating disorder. The best step is to...','["make jokes about their body", "post about it online", "tell them to just eat more", "express concern and encourage them to talk to a trusted adult or doctor"]'::jsonb,3,'Eating disorders are medical conditions that need professional help.','original'),
('115.27.b.6.E',3,'A protective factor against suicide is...','["strong connections with family, friends and caring adults", "easy access to harmful items", "isolation from others", "refusing all help"]'::jsonb,0,'Connectedness and support lower risk.','original'),
('115.27.b.6.E',3,'If a friend talks about wanting to die, you should...','["keep the secret to protect them", "take it seriously and tell a trusted adult right away", "tell them to stop being dramatic", "wait to see if it passes"]'::jsonb,1,'Always tell a trusted adult; this can save a life.','original'),
('115.27.b.6.F',3,'Which healthy strategy helps a teen who feels overwhelming sadness stay safe?','["hiding the feelings", "using substances", "reaching out to a trusted adult or counselor", "harming oneself"]'::jsonb,2,'Seeking support is a protective strategy.','original'),
('115.27.b.6.F',3,'A protective factor against self-harming behavior is...','["secrecy and shame", "ignoring feelings", "constant isolation", "having healthy coping skills and caring support people"]'::jsonb,3,'Coping skills and support reduce risk.','original'),
('115.27.b.6.G',3,'In the United States, the 988 Suicide and Crisis Lifeline can be reached by...','["calling or texting 988", "mailing a letter", "posting on social media", "waiting for school to open"]'::jsonb,0,'988 offers free, confidential support.','original'),
('115.27.b.6.G',3,'Using a crisis line such as 988 can reduce suicide risk because it provides...','["a ride to school", "immediate support from a trained counselor", "a diagnosis by text only", "a guaranteed cure"]'::jsonb,1,'Trained counselors help people stay safe.','original'),
('115.27.b.7.A',3,'On a food label, the serving size matters because all the other numbers are based on...','["the weight of the package only", "the whole box", "one serving", "the price"]'::jsonb,2,'Nutrition facts are listed per serving.','original'),
('115.27.b.7.A',3,'A healthy choice on a food label is a food that is...','["highest in added sugar", "lowest in fiber", "highest in saturated fat", "lower in added sugar and sodium"]'::jsonb,3,'Limiting added sugar and sodium supports health.','original'),
('115.27.b.7.B',3,'A personal dietary plan should include...','["a variety of fruits, vegetables, whole grains and protein", "only one food group", "mostly energy drinks", "no breakfast ever"]'::jsonb,0,'Variety supplies needed nutrients.','original'),
('115.27.b.7.B',3,'Which plan is the best start for a teen creating a healthy dietary plan?','["avoid water", "plan balanced meals and snacks for the week", "eat only fast food", "skip meals to lose weight fast"]'::jsonb,1,'Balanced planning supports growth.','original'),
('115.27.b.7.C',3,'At a party with many snacks, a healthy strategy is to...','["skip eating all day beforehand", "drink only soda", "choose fruit or veggies first and drink water", "eat until you are sick"]'::jsonb,2,'Healthy choices are possible in social settings.','original'),
('115.27.b.7.C',3,'When ordering from a restaurant menu, a healthier beverage choice is...','["a large sweet soda", "a sugary energy drink", "a milkshake every time", "water or low-fat milk"]'::jsonb,3,'Water and milk are lower in added sugar.','original'),
('115.27.b.8.A',3,'Regular physical activity and good nutrition help lower the risk of...','["chronic diseases such as heart disease and type 2 diabetes", "growing taller than the average", "forgetting homework", "getting a sunburn"]'::jsonb,0,'Healthy habits reduce chronic disease risk.','original'),
('115.27.b.8.A',3,'How does good nutrition affect quality of life?','["it lowers school attendance", "it gives energy and supports concentration and mood", "it removes the need for sleep", "it prevents all illness"]'::jsonb,1,'Nutrition supports daily function.','original'),
('115.27.b.8.B',3,'To maintain a healthy weight, a person generally balances...','["sleep and homework", "water and salt only", "calories taken in with calories burned", "heart rate and temperature"]'::jsonb,2,'Energy balance is calories in vs. calories out.','original'),
('115.27.b.8.B',3,'If a teen eats more calories than their body uses over time, the extra energy is stored as...','["bone", "extra height", "muscle only", "body fat"]'::jsonb,3,'Unused calories are stored as fat.','original'),
('115.27.b.8.C',3,'The CDC recommends that school-age youth get at least how much physical activity per day?','["60 minutes", "3 hours", "15 minutes", "5 minutes"]'::jsonb,0,'Youth need about 60 minutes of moderate to vigorous activity daily.','original'),
('115.27.b.8.C',3,'A student wants to track daily steps and heart rate for a fitness plan. Which technology helps?','["a flashlight", "a fitness tracker or smartwatch", "a printed menu", "a calculator with no sensors"]'::jsonb,1,'Wearables record activity data.','original'),
('115.27.b.9.A',3,'A SMART fitness goal is...','["''do more than everyone''", "''be perfect''", "specific and measurable, such as ''jog 20 minutes three days a week''", "''get fit someday''"]'::jsonb,2,'Specific, measurable goals can be tracked.','original'),
('115.27.b.9.A',3,'To examine progress toward a physical activity goal, a teen should...','["compare only to celebrities", "quit after one missed day", "never measure anything", "track results regularly and adjust the plan"]'::jsonb,3,'Tracking shows progress.','original'),
('115.27.b.9.B',3,'An advertisement claims a powder will give ''instant abs with no exercise.'' A smart consumer should...','["question the claim and check reliable health sources", "trust it because it has a famous endorsement", "assume all ads tell the truth", "buy it at once"]'::jsonb,0,'Media can mislead buying decisions.','original'),
('115.27.b.9.B',3,'Influencers on social media often promote supplements. This is an example of media...','["teaching anatomy", "influencing buying decisions", "preventing disease", "banning products"]'::jsonb,1,'Marketing shapes what people buy.','original'),
('115.27.b.10.A',3,'Which habits reduce the risk of obesity and heart disease?','["long hours of inactivity", "frequent fast food", "moderate physical activity and healthy eating", "skipping sleep"]'::jsonb,2,'Activity and diet prevent chronic conditions.','original'),
('115.27.b.10.A',3,'A diet high in processed foods and low in vegetables most increases the risk of...','["a cold", "a sunburn", "a broken bone", "chronic conditions such as type 2 diabetes"]'::jsonb,3,'Poor diet raises chronic disease risk.','original'),
('115.27.b.10.B',3,'A risk factor that can lead to heart disease is...','["tobacco use", "getting enough sleep", "regular exercise", "drinking water"]'::jsonb,0,'Tobacco damages the heart and blood vessels.','original'),
('115.27.b.10.B',3,'A strategy to reduce the risk of chronic conditions is...','["smoking only socially", "scheduling regular checkups and staying active", "avoiding all doctors", "sitting all day"]'::jsonb,1,'Prevention starts with healthy habits.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
