from (values
('115.27.b.10.C',3,'A digital resource for planning healthy eating is...','["a random meme page", "a celebrity gossip site", "a nutrition app or the government''s MyPlate website", "an unlicensed supplement ad"]'::jsonb,2,'MyPlate offers evidence-based help.','original'),
('115.27.b.10.C',3,'A community resource for staying physically active is...','["a vending machine", "a video game arcade only", "a drive-through restaurant", "a local park or recreation center"]'::jsonb,3,'Public spaces support activity.','original'),
('115.27.b.10.D',3,'Compared with highly processed packaged snacks, fresh or minimally processed foods usually have...','["fewer additives and less added sugar and sodium", "more added salt", "more artificial colors", "no vitamins"]'::jsonb,0,'Fresh foods retain more nutrients.','original'),
('115.27.b.10.D',3,'Which meal is the more minimally processed option?','["chicken nuggets with sweet sauce", "a baked chicken breast with steamed broccoli", "instant noodle cups with seasoning packets", "a boxed cake mix"]'::jsonb,1,'Fresh, simply prepared foods are minimally processed.','original'),
('115.27.b.11',3,'Which safety skill helps prevent a house fire?','["overloading outlets", "removing the smoke detector battery", "never leaving cooking food unattended", "storing oily rags near a heater"]'::jsonb,2,'Staying near the stove prevents kitchen fires.','original'),
('115.27.b.11',3,'To prevent unintentional injury while riding a bike, a teen should...','["wear headphones in both ears", "ride without lights at night", "ignore traffic signs", "wear a properly fitted helmet"]'::jsonb,3,'Helmets protect against head injury.','original'),
('115.27.b.12.A',3,'A benefit of avoiding gangs and weapons is...','["lower risk of injury, arrest and violence", "better ticket prices", "more free time at night", "faster internet"]'::jsonb,0,'Avoiding violence protects safety.','original'),
('115.27.b.12.A',3,'Which is a warning sign of human trafficking involvement?','["a family vacation", "an adult controlling a young person''s money and communications", "a part-time job at a store", "a student joining a club"]'::jsonb,1,'Control and isolation are warning signs.','original'),
('115.27.b.12.B',3,'A safe haven is a...','["dark alley", "private home with no adults", "designated place where a person in danger can go for help", "random store room"]'::jsonb,2,'Safe havens offer protection.','original'),
('115.27.b.12.B',3,'Which could be a designated safe haven location in a community?','["an unknown party house", "a locked storage unit", "an empty lot", "a fire station or police station"]'::jsonb,3,'Public safety buildings offer help.','original'),
('115.27.b.12.C',3,'A firearm in a home is especially dangerous when it is...','["stored loaded and unlocked", "stored apart from ammunition", "locked and unloaded", "kept in a safe"]'::jsonb,0,'Unsecured loaded guns cause tragedies.','original'),
('115.27.b.12.C',3,'Which statement about weapons is true?','["Only adults can be injured", "Handling a weapon without training can cause serious injury", "Toy weapons and real weapons are identical in danger", "A weapon is safe if it is never touched"]'::jsonb,1,'Weapons can cause serious harm when misused.','original'),
('115.27.b.12.D',3,'A rule that prohibits weapons at school exists to...','["reduce class time", "increase detention", "keep students and staff safe", "limit free speech"]'::jsonb,2,'Compliance protects everyone.','original'),
('115.27.b.12.D',3,'If a student sees a classmate with a weapon at school, the best action is to...','["confront the classmate", "ignore it", "post about it online", "tell a trusted adult or school official immediately"]'::jsonb,3,'Reporting prevents harm.','original'),
('115.27.b.12.E',3,'Which belongs in a personal safety plan?','["emergency numbers and a safe exit route", "a social media password list for everyone", "a list of rumors", "the school menu"]'::jsonb,0,'Plans prepare you to act quickly.','original'),
('115.27.b.13.A',3,'If someone online asks a teen to send a private photo, the teen should...','["keep it secret", "refuse, block the person and tell a trusted adult", "send it just once", "ask for money first"]'::jsonb,1,'Resist and report inappropriate requests.','original'),
('115.27.b.13.A',3,'A strategy to resist inappropriate digital communication is to...','["share the message widely", "meet the person to talk", "not respond and save evidence for a trusted adult", "reply with personal details"]'::jsonb,2,'Do not engage; keep evidence.','original'),
('115.27.b.13.B',3,'A consequence of sharing inappropriate images online can be...','["guaranteed deletion", "more privacy", "better grades", "lasting harm to reputation and possible legal trouble"]'::jsonb,3,'Online content can spread and persist.','original'),
('115.27.b.13.B',3,'Posting something hurtful about a classmate can lead to...','["school discipline and harm to others", "no consequences", "automatic popularity forever", "a school award"]'::jsonb,0,'Cyber behavior has real consequences.','original'),
('115.27.b.13.C',3,'A good way to protect your identity online is to...','["share your password with friends", "use strong, unique passwords and keep personal details private", "post your address", "use the same password everywhere"]'::jsonb,1,'Strong passwords and privacy protect identity.','original'),
('115.27.b.13.C',3,'Which online action helps protect personal identity?','["posting a school schedule publicly", "accepting every follow request", "adjusting privacy settings on accounts", "clicking unknown links"]'::jsonb,2,'Privacy settings limit exposure.','original'),
('115.27.b.13.D',3,'Predators may use the internet to recruit victims by...','["posting weather updates", "sharing recipes", "sending class assignments", "pretending to be a friend and offering gifts or attention"]'::jsonb,3,'Grooming relies on building false trust.','original'),
('115.27.b.13.D',3,'A sign that an online ''friend'' may be trying to manipulate a teen is...','["pushing them to keep secrets from parents", "sharing a school project", "offering study tips", "asking about favorite music"]'::jsonb,0,'Secrecy is a manipulation tactic.','original'),
('115.27.b.13.E',3,'In many states, cyberbullying can be...','["always legal", "a crime or lead to legal consequences", "a school honor", "ignored by courts"]'::jsonb,1,'Laws can apply to cyberbullying.','original'),
('115.27.b.13.E',3,'A legal consequence of sending threats online can be...','["a certificate", "a scholarship", "criminal charges or juvenile court involvement", "extra recess"]'::jsonb,2,'Threats can be criminal.','original'),
('115.27.b.14.A',3,'Which is a form of emotional family violence?','["help with homework", "a chore chart", "family game night", "constant insults, threats or controlling behavior"]'::jsonb,3,'Emotional abuse includes insults and control.','original'),
('115.27.b.14.A',3,'Family violence can include...','["physical, mental and emotional harm", "only strangers'' behavior", "only arguments in public", "only broken windows"]'::jsonb,0,'Violence takes many forms.','original'),
('115.27.b.14.B',3,'A serious effect of bullying and cyberbullying on a victim can be...','["higher grades", "depression, anxiety, or thoughts of suicide", "improved health", "greater self-confidence"]'::jsonb,1,'Bullying can seriously harm mental health.','original'),
('115.27.b.14.B',3,'Harassment can have long-term effects such as...','["more friends", "better focus", "withdrawal, poor sleep and low self-esteem", "improved appetite"]'::jsonb,2,'These are common effects.','original'),
('115.27.b.14.C',3,'A witness who sees bullying should...','["join in", "ignore it", "film it for fun", "report it to a trusted adult or the school"]'::jsonb,3,'Reporting is the responsible choice.','original'),
('115.27.b.14.C',3,'Why is it important to report cyberbullying?','["it helps stop the harm and protect the victim", "so the bully gets famous", "to start another fight", "to avoid school"]'::jsonb,0,'Reports lead to intervention.','original'),
('115.27.b.14.D',3,'Harassment becomes more serious when it is...','["an apology", "repeated or targets a person''s identity", "a one-time friendly joke", "an invitation"]'::jsonb,1,'Repeated or identity-based targeting is serious.','original'),
('115.27.b.14.D',3,'Which behavior is a form of bullying?','["asking for a ride", "helping with homework", "repeatedly spreading rumors to hurt someone", "working on a group project"]'::jsonb,2,'Repeated harmful behavior is bullying.','original'),
('115.27.b.14.E',3,'A prevention strategy for bullying at school is...','["encouraging gossip", "ignoring problems", "punishing the victim", "building a positive, inclusive culture and teaching empathy"]'::jsonb,3,'Prevention starts with culture.','original'),
('115.27.b.14.E',3,'An effective intervention if you see someone being bullied is to...','["support the target and get help from an adult", "spread the video", "laugh along", "retaliate with insults"]'::jsonb,0,'Safe, supportive intervention helps.','original')
