('115.27.b.14.F',3,'Seeking advice from a trusted adult before making a big decision helps because it...','["takes away your choices", "gives you other perspectives and information", "means you cannot think for yourself", "guarantees you are right"]'::jsonb,1,'Advice improves decision-making.','original'),
('115.27.b.14.F',3,'Which person is a good source of feedback on a tough problem?','["someone who gossips", "a person who pressures you", "a counselor, parent or mentor you trust", "a stranger online"]'::jsonb,2,'Trusted adults give reliable guidance.','original'),
('115.27.b.15.A',3,'Taking a prescription medicine prescribed for someone else is...','["always helpful", "okay for headaches", "safe if it looks the same", "inappropriate and can be dangerous"]'::jsonb,3,'Prescriptions are made for the patient.','original'),
('115.27.b.15.A',3,'Which is appropriate use of an over-the-counter drug?','["taking the amount listed on the label", "doubling the dose to feel better faster", "sharing it with classmates", "mixing with alcohol"]'::jsonb,0,'Follow label directions.','original'),
('115.27.b.15.B',3,'Antibiotics are prescribed to treat...','["viral colds", "bacterial infections", "broken bones", "sunburn"]'::jsonb,1,'Antibiotics fight bacteria, not viruses.','original'),
('115.27.b.15.B',3,'Opioid prescription drugs are mainly used for...','["improving test scores", "gaining muscle", "pain management under a doctor''s care", "increasing energy"]'::jsonb,2,'Opioids treat severe pain and are risky.','original'),
('115.27.b.15.C',3,'On an over-the-counter drug label, the ''Active ingredient'' section tells you...','["how much it costs", "where it was made", "who sells it", "which ingredient makes the medicine work"]'::jsonb,3,'The Drug Facts label lists active ingredients.','original'),
('115.27.b.15.C',3,'The warnings section on an OTC label tells you...','["when not to use the medicine and possible side effects", "the price", "the best flavor", "the shipping date"]'::jsonb,0,'Warnings help prevent harm.','original'),
('115.27.b.15.D',3,'Substance misuse and addiction can harm...','["only adults", "health, relationships and school performance", "only strangers", "no one"]'::jsonb,1,'Addiction affects every part of life.','original'),
('115.27.b.15.D',3,'A person who is addicted to vaping nicotine may experience...','["greater lung capacity", "less stress", "cravings and withdrawal when they try to stop", "improved sleep"]'::jsonb,2,'Nicotine is highly addictive.','original'),
('115.27.b.16.A',3,'A long-term health consequence of tobacco use is...','["improved stamina", "stronger bones", "clearer skin", "lung and heart disease"]'::jsonb,3,'Tobacco causes serious disease.','original'),
('115.27.b.16.A',3,'A short-term effect of alcohol on a teen''s body is...','["impaired judgment and coordination", "better memory", "faster reaction time", "increased focus"]'::jsonb,0,'Alcohol slows the brain.','original'),
('115.27.b.16.B',3,'Choosing alternative activities such as sports or clubs can help teens avoid drug use because they...','["increase boredom", "provide healthy outlets, friends and a sense of purpose", "require money for drugs", "isolate you"]'::jsonb,1,'Positive activities support well-being.','original'),
('115.27.b.16.B',3,'Which is a healthy alternative to substance use for coping with stress?','["using vaping products", "drinking energy drinks all night", "joining a team or creative club", "skipping school"]'::jsonb,2,'Healthy activities reduce risk.','original'),
('115.27.b.16.C',3,'In Texas, it is illegal for a minor to...','["get a library card", "join a sports team", "attend school", "possess or buy alcohol or tobacco products"]'::jsonb,3,'Laws prohibit minors from alcohol and tobacco.','original'),
('115.27.b.16.C',3,'A legal consequence of using illegal drugs as a teen can be...','["juvenile detention, fines or a criminal record", "a scholarship", "extra privileges", "a driver''s license at 12"]'::jsonb,0,'Drug use can lead to legal trouble.','original'),
('115.27.b.17.A',3,'A treatment option for substance abuse is...','["ignoring it", "counseling, support groups or supervised treatment programs", "isolating at home", "using more substances"]'::jsonb,1,'Professional treatment helps recovery.','original'),
('115.27.b.17.A',3,'Which of these helps a person recovering from addiction?','["losing friends", "secrecy and shame", "a strong support system and professional care", "access to substances"]'::jsonb,2,'Support improves outcomes.','original'),
('115.27.b.17.B',3,'A sign that a person may be misusing substances is...','["getting a haircut", "taking a vacation", "joining the debate team", "sudden changes in grades, friends and mood"]'::jsonb,3,'Sudden changes can signal a problem.','original'),
('115.27.b.17.B',3,'Which behavior may signal drug use?','["unexplained secrecy and loss of interest in favorite activities", "studying more", "practicing an instrument", "eating breakfast"]'::jsonb,0,'These changes can be signs.','original'),
('115.27.b.17.C',3,'A teen who needs help with a friend''s drug use can talk to...','["no one", "a school counselor or trusted adult", "other users", "a stranger"]'::jsonb,1,'Trusted adults provide help.','original'),
('115.27.b.17.C',3,'In the United States, someone seeking free, confidential help for substance use can call...','["a random number", "a pizza restaurant", "the SAMHSA National Helpline at 1-800-662-4357", "a car dealer"]'::jsonb,2,'SAMHSA offers a 24/7 helpline.','original'),
('115.27.b.18.A',3,'Peer pressure to try alcohol is best resisted by...','["giving in to fit in", "waiting to see what happens", "daring a friend to do it first", "saying no firmly and leaving the situation"]'::jsonb,3,'Refusal skills protect health.','original'),
('115.27.b.18.A',3,'Positive peer influence regarding drug use includes...','["friends who encourage healthy choices", "friends who dare you", "friends who hide drugs", "friends who laugh at those who refuse"]'::jsonb,0,'Good friends support healthy decisions.','original'),
('115.27.b.18.B',3,'A social influence that can increase tobacco use among teens is...','["learning about health risks", "seeing family members or friends use it", "joining sports", "reading warning labels"]'::jsonb,1,'Role models and peers shape behavior.','original'),
('115.27.b.18.B',3,'Advertising for vaping products often targets teens with...','["doctor recommendations", "free health classes", "flavors and social media marketing", "warning labels only"]'::jsonb,2,'Marketing influences use.','original'),
('115.27.b.18.C',3,'A drug that is a stimulant tends to...','["lower the heart rate", "slow breathing in all cases", "make a person fall asleep", "speed up the central nervous system"]'::jsonb,3,'Stimulants increase alertness and heart rate.','original'),
('115.27.b.18.C',3,'Depressants such as alcohol generally...','["slow down brain activity", "speed up reaction time", "improve memory", "increase alertness"]'::jsonb,0,'Depressants slow the nervous system.','original'),
('115.27.b.18.D',3,'If a teen suspects a friend is abusing drugs, a way to report it is to...','["confront the dealer", "tell a parent, school counselor or administrator", "post online", "tell only other students"]'::jsonb,1,'Adults can get help safely.','original'),
('115.27.b.18.D',3,'Reporting suspected drug abuse to a trusted adult is an example of...','["breaking a law", "betraying a friend", "using a support system to help a friend", "starting a fight"]'::jsonb,2,'Reporting is caring, not betrayal.','original'),
('115.27.b.19',3,'The best way to prevent alcohol, tobacco and drug problems is to...','["wait until you are older to start experimenting", "use only on weekends", "try them once", "avoid using them and build refusal skills"]'::jsonb,3,'Prevention means not starting.','original'),
('115.27.b.19',3,'Critical thinking about a vaping advertisement means asking...','["who made the ad and what they want me to do", "how many likes it has", "how many colors it has", "what size the font is"]'::jsonb,0,'Evaluating messages helps prevention.','original'),
('115.27.b.20.A',3,'Which of the following best describes friendship?','["intense physical attraction only", "mutual care, trust and enjoying time together", "financial agreement", "legal commitment"]'::jsonb,1,'Friendship is based on trust and care.','original'),
('115.27.b.20.A',3,'Marriage differs from dating in that marriage is...','["a school activity", "required by age 16", "a legal, long-term commitment", "always a friendship"]'::jsonb,2,'Marriage is a legal commitment.','original'),
('115.27.b.20.B',3,'Healthy dating relationships often begin as...','["forced pairings", "unknown strangers", "online-only contact with no knowledge", "friendships built on trust and respect"]'::jsonb,3,'Friendship provides a foundation.','original')
